    "offices": {
      "President": "Elected by popular vote for a four-year term, with a run-off between the top two if no candidate wins more than half the valid votes; a president may run again only after a term out of office. The president is head of state and head of government.",
      "Chamber of Deputies": "All 155 deputies are elected for four years in 28 multi-member districts of three to eight seats by open-list proportional representation (d'Hondt). Together with the Senate it makes the laws.",
      "Senate": "The 50 senators serve staggered eight-year terms: about half are elected at each general election, in 16 regional constituencies of two to five seats under the same proportional rules. It shares law-making with the Chamber of Deputies."
    }
